How it is tested
----------------

A Docker lab with emulated disks, and the tests of the API against real
filesystems, are in a separate repository:

    https://github.com/paleka/snapraid-lab

The screenshots of the Storage page are there too. No picture is added to
this repository, to keep the difference from the original project small.


Packages and releases
---------------------

The package is named 'snapraid-daemon-storage', and it declares that it
replaces and conflicts with 'snapraid-daemon', the package of the original
project. The program, the service and the configuration file are the same.

A release is made pushing an annotated tag on the 'storage' branch. The tag is the
version of SnapRAID Daemon the branch is based on, followed by the number of
the release of the fork:

    git tag -a v2.2.s1 -m "SnapRAID Daemon with the Storage page 2.2.s1"
    git push origin v2.2.s1

The Release workflow then builds the source package, the .deb and the .rpm,
and publishes them with their checksums. The tags of the original project
have to be in the fork, because the version is taken from them:

    git push origin --tags


Keeping up with the original project
------------------------------------

    git remote add upstream https://github.com/amadvance/snapraid-daemon.git
    git fetch upstream
    git checkout master && git merge --ff-only upstream/master
    git checkout storage && git rebase master
